[] This was rather distressing. Has anyone else had this problem ?
[] Have I been done for by a new `security' feature ?

NetHack checks the time stamp of "critical" files to see if they are
newer than itself.  this is a measure of security because older saved
games, for example, aren't guaranteed compatible.

altho this doesn't help you now, pl9 bones/saves are compatible with
pl10.  however, you do have to update the timestamp of those files.
on Unix that's "touch bones* save/*" or something similar ...

